## Workflow

- Required plugins: flow@flow-skeleton and superpowers. If /flow: skills
  are missing at session start, say so to the owner before working.
- Non-trivial work goes through the flow plugin: /flow:spec → owner
  approval → /flow:implement (fresh session) → /flow:accept → owner
  accepts. Trivial changes (one-sentence diff, no dependents) skip the
  lifecycle.
- When the owner requests non-trivial work without mentioning flow,
  offer to start /flow:spec before writing any code — one line, not a
  lecture. If the owner declines, proceed normally.
- Worktree sessions: auto memory is shared across the repository's
  worktrees, but openspec/ and CHANGELOG.md still carry the work state;
  this file carries only standing facts and the bounded Current state
  block. Merge back to the trunk when a phase completes.
- If the flow plugin is unavailable in this session (cloud VM, fresh
  machine), follow the lifecycle shape manually: openspec change → owner
  approval → TDD implementation on a branch → full checks + fresh-context
  review → owner accepts.
- Commit locally as the work goes. Publishing follows the authority
  profile recorded in this file, when one is; with none recorded, ask
  before pushing. Merging a PR, the release tag and a production deploy
  stay the owner's.

